# Contract: `ApiClient.downloadFile` (`lib/core/network/api_client.dart`)

Extends `ApiClient` (F000/RF01, already extended by RF04's `sseStream()`) in place. `call()`/`sseStream()` are
unchanged. This is a `core/network/` addition, not export-specific — any future signed-URL-download unit
reuses it as-is (research.md R1).

```dart
Future<Either<Failure, Uint8List>> downloadFile(
  String function, {
  List<String>? pathSegments,
  Map<String, dynamic>? queryParameters,
  AuthMode authMode = AuthMode.userSession,
}) async {
  final baseUrl = dotenv.env['FUNCTIONS_BASE_URL'] ?? '';
  final segments = [function, ...?pathSegments];
  final url = '$baseUrl/${segments.join('/')}';
  final bearer = authMode == AuthMode.anonKey
      ? _anonKey
      : (await _tokenStorage.readAccessToken() ?? '');

  try {
    // Leg 1 — our own backend function. Same apikey/Authorization headers every other `call()` already
    // sends. `followRedirects: false` + accepting <400 via `validateStatus` means a 302 lands here as a
    // normal response object instead of being auto-followed (which would forward these headers to Storage).
    final redirectResponse = await _dio.request<void>(
      url,
      queryParameters: queryParameters,
      options: Options(
        method: 'GET',
        headers: {'apikey': _anonKey, 'Authorization': 'Bearer $bearer'},
        followRedirects: false,
        validateStatus: (status) => status != null && status < 400,
      ),
    );

    final location = redirectResponse.headers.value('location');
    if (redirectResponse.statusCode != 302 || location == null) {
      return const Left(
        ValidationFailure(message: 'Malformed response: expected a 302 redirect', requestId: ''),
      );
    }

    // Leg 2 — the signed Storage URL. Deliberately NO apikey/Authorization headers: the signed URL already
    // carries its own short-lived auth via query parameters, and forwarding this app's own credentials to a
    // third-party host they were never scoped for is an unnecessary exposure (research.md R1).
    final fileResponse = await _dio.request<List<int>>(
      location,
      options: Options(method: 'GET', responseType: ResponseType.bytes),
    );

    return Right(Uint8List.fromList(fileResponse.data ?? const []));
  } on DioException catch (e) {
    // Leg 1 failures (our backend's own {code, message, retryable} envelope) map through the exact same
    // `_mapException` every other call() site already uses. Leg 2 failures (the storage host never speaks
    // this app's error envelope — a 403/404 from an expired signed URL, a dropped connection mid-download)
    // have no `{code, message, retryable}` body to parse, so they fall through `_mapException`'s own
    // no-JSON-body branch and resolve to the same retryable `NetworkOfflineFailure`/`NetworkTimeoutFailure`
    // it already synthesizes for a connection-level failure — never a new, undocumented Failure subtype.
    return Left(_mapException(e));
  }
}
```

- Exactly two network round-trips per call, in sequence — never more (no following of a second redirect; a
  Storage response that itself redirects again is treated as leg 2's own non-2xx failure via `_mapException`,
  since `_dio.request<List<int>>` here keeps `dio`'s default `followRedirects: true` only for leg 2, where no
  credential is being forwarded in the first place, so a further redirect being auto-followed is harmless).
- No `unwrapData`-style parameter and no `body` parameter — `GET /export/{jobId}/download` takes no request
  body, and the return shape is always raw bytes, never a `{"data": ...}` JSON envelope.

## Test scenarios this contract owns

| # | Scenario | Expected |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Leg 1 returns `302` with a valid `location` header; leg 2 returns `200` with bytes | `Right(Uint8List)` containing exactly those bytes |
| 2 | Leg 1 returns `200` (no redirect at all — a contract-violating response) | `Left(ValidationFailure)` |
| 3 | Leg 1 returns `302` with no `location` header | `Left(ValidationFailure)` |
| 4 | Leg 1 throws a `DioException` with `{code: 'AUTH_EXPIRED', ...}` in its response body | `Left(AuthExpiredFailure)` — identical mapping to `call()`'s own `AUTH_EXPIRED` handling |
| 5 | Leg 1 succeeds (302 + location); leg 2 throws a `DioException` with `type: connectionTimeout` | `Left(NetworkTimeoutFailure)` — the storage-leg failure, not confused with a leg-1 failure |
| 6 | Leg 1 succeeds; leg 2 throws a `DioException` with no `response` at all (expired/garbage signed URL rejected at the transport level) | `Left(NetworkOfflineFailure)` |
| 7 | `downloadFile` called with `queryParameters: {'format': 'raw'}` | leg 1's request URL carries `?format=raw` verbatim |

# Contract: `ExportRepository` / `ExportFileRepository`

`lib/features/export/domain/repositories/export_repository.dart`,
`lib/features/export/domain/repositories/export_file_repository.dart`, implemented by
`lib/features/export/data/export_repository_impl.dart`/`export_file_repository_impl.dart`.

```dart
abstract class ExportRepository {
  Future<Either<Failure, String>> create({required DateTime? periodStart, required DateTime? periodEnd});
  Future<Either<Failure, ExportJob>> status(String jobId);
  Future<Either<Failure, Uint8List>> download({required String jobId, required ExportFormat format});
}

abstract class ExportFileRepository {
  Future<Either<Failure, Unit>> share({required Uint8List bytes, required ExportFormat format});
}
```

## `ExportRepositoryImpl.create` — request shape

```dart
await _apiClient.call(
  'export-summary-create',
  method: 'POST',
  body: {
    'periodStart': periodStart?.toUtc().toIso8601String(),  // explicit null, never omitted — both keys are
    'periodEnd': periodEnd?.toUtc().toIso8601String(),      // in the OpenAPI schema's `required` list even
    'includeNarrative': true,                               // though both are `nullable: true`
  },
);
```

Parses `data.jobId` (string) from the `202` response; `data.status` is always `'pending'` at this point and is
not separately parsed (the first `status()` poll re-derives the real `ExportJob` immediately after).
`EXPORT_EMPTY_PERIOD` (400) is mapped by the existing, shared `ErrorMapper.fromResponse` → `Left
(ExportEmptyPeriodFailure)` — no export-specific error parsing needed.

## `ExportRepositoryImpl.status` — response shape

```dart
await _apiClient.call('export-status-get', method: 'GET', pathSegments: [jobId]);
```

Parses the full `ExportJob` (`data.jobId`/`data.status`/`data.narrativeStatus`/`data.entryCount`/
`data.errorCode`/`data.narrativeErrorCode`/`data.downloadAvailable`) — every field in the OpenAPI schema's own
`required` list, all nullable except `jobId`/`status`/`narrativeStatus`/`downloadAvailable`. `status`'s wire
value `data_ready` parses to `ExportJobStatus.dataReady` via an explicit lookup table (not `.byName`, since
Dart enum names cannot contain an underscore the way the wire value does) — every other enum
(`ExportJobStatus`'s other four values, all of `NarrativeStatus`) parses via `.byName` as usual.

## `ExportRepositoryImpl.download` — delegates to `ApiClient.downloadFile`

```dart
await _apiClient.downloadFile(
  'export-download-get',
  pathSegments: [jobId],
  queryParameters: {'format': format.name},  // 'pdf' | 'raw'
);
```

No response parsing — `contracts/http-client-download-extension.md` already returns raw `Uint8List`.

## Silent-refresh-and-retry — identical shape across all three methods

```dart
Future<Either<Failure, T>> _retryAfterSilentRefresh<T>(Future<Either<Failure, T>> Function() retry) async {
  final refreshed = await _sessionRepository.refresh();
  return refreshed.match(
    (_) => Future.value(const Left(AuthExpiredFailure(message: 'Session could not be renewed', requestId: ''))),
    (_) => retry(),
  );
}
```

Copied verbatim from `EntriesRepositoryImpl` (RF07) — exactly one retry; a second `AuthExpiredFailure` after
that retry is returned as-is, never a loop.

## `ExportFileRepositoryImpl.share` — behavior

```dart
Future<Either<Failure, Unit>> share({required Uint8List bytes, required ExportFormat format}) async {
  try {
    final dir = await getTemporaryDirectory();
    final extension = format == ExportFormat.pdf ? 'pdf' : 'json';
    final name = format == ExportFormat.pdf ? 'cerne-resumo' : 'cerne-dados';
    final file = File('${dir.path}/$name.$extension');
    await file.writeAsBytes(bytes, flush: true);
    await Share.shareXFiles([XFile(file.path)]);
    return const Right(unit);
  } catch (_) {
    return const Left(NetworkTimeoutFailure(message: 'Falha ao salvar/compartilhar o arquivo.', requestId: ''));
  }
}
```

A `share_plus` cancel (the user dismissing the OS share sheet without picking a target) is reported by the
package as a normal, non-throwing `ShareResult` — never reaches the `catch` above, and is treated as success
(`Right(unit)`): the file *was* produced and offered; whether the user then chose to save it is outside this
unit's concern (Assumptions: "this unit is not responsible for building a custom in-app file viewer").

## Test scenarios this contract owns

| # | Scenario | Expected |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | `create()` — backend returns `202 {jobId: 'abc'}` | `Right('abc')` |
| 2 | `create()` — backend returns `400 {code: 'EXPORT_EMPTY_PERIOD', ...}` | `Left(ExportEmptyPeriodFailure)` |
| 3 | `create()` — backend returns `504 {code: 'NETWORK_TIMEOUT', ...}` (or a transport-level timeout) | `Left(NetworkTimeoutFailure)` |
| 4 | `status()` — backend returns `{status: 'data_ready', narrativeStatus: 'processing', downloadAvailable: true, ...}` | `Right(ExportJob(status: dataReady, narrativeStatus: processing, ...))` |
| 5 | `status()` — malformed body (missing a required field) | `Left(ValidationFailure)` |
| 6 | `create()`/`status()`/`download()` — first attempt `AuthExpiredFailure`, `SessionRepository.refresh()` succeeds, retried call succeeds | the retried call's own `Right(...)` |
| 7 | Same as 6, but `refresh()` itself fails | `Left(AuthExpiredFailure)` — exactly one retry, no loop |
| 8 | `download()` — `ApiClient.downloadFile` returns `Right(bytes)` | `Right(bytes)` unchanged |
| 9 | `ExportFileRepositoryImpl.share()` — `path_provider`/file-write succeeds, `Share.shareXFiles` resolves normally (including a user-cancelled share) | `Right(unit)` |
| 10 | `ExportFileRepositoryImpl.share()` — the file write throws (e.g. disk full) | `Left(NetworkTimeoutFailure)` (retryable) |

# Contract: Records header's download icon (`lib/features/records/presentation/pages/records_page.dart`)

Extends `_Header`/`_RecordsPageState` in place (FR-001/FR-002/FR-011). `RecordsBloc`/`RecordsEvent`/
`RecordsState` are unchanged — no new event, no new field (research.md R8).

```dart
class _Header extends StatelessWidget {
  const _Header({required this.onExportPressed});
  final VoidCallback onExportPressed;

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    return Padding(
      // ...unchanged back-arrow + title...
      child: Row(
        children: [
          /* back arrow, title — unchanged */
          IconButton(
            onPressed: onExportPressed,                              // was: () {} (inert placeholder)
            icon: const Icon(Icons.download_outlined, color: DesignTokens.colorTextPrimary),
          ),
        ],
      ),
    );
  }
}
```

```dart
class _RecordsPageState extends State<RecordsPage> {
  bool _isOpeningExportSheet = false;   // NEW

  Future<void> _openExportSheet(BuildContext context) async {
    if (_isOpeningExportSheet) return;                                   // FR-011
    _isOpeningExportSheet = true;
    final state = context.read<RecordsBloc>().state;
    final dateRange = state is RecordsLoaded ? state.dateRange : DateRangeOption.allTime;
    final bounds = dateRange.boundsAt(DateTime.now());                    // RF06's own pure extension, reused
    await showModalBottomSheet<void>(
      context: context,
      isScrollControlled: true,
      builder: (_) => ExportSheet(periodStart: bounds.from, periodEnd: bounds.to),
    );
    if (mounted) _isOpeningExportSheet = false;
  }

  // build(): `_Header(onExportPressed: () => _openExportSheet(context))` replaces the bare `_Header()`.
}
```

- `_isOpeningExportSheet` resets to `false` only after `showModalBottomSheet`'s `Future` resolves (the sheet
  was dismissed) and only if the widget is still mounted — a second tap while the sheet is open is already
  physically blocked by the modal barrier Flutter itself draws, so this flag's only real job is absorbing a
  double-tap in the brief window before the sheet has finished animating in.
- No change to `RecordsBloc`'s own filter state: reading `context.read<RecordsBloc>().state` here is a
  one-time snapshot at tap time, never a `watch` — `_Header` itself stays a plain, non-rebuilding
  `StatelessWidget` with respect to `RecordsBloc` (unaffected by RF05, same as `_SearchBar`'s existing
  `context.watch<RecordsBloc>()` usage for the filter icon's own highlight state, which this unit does not
  touch).

## Test scenarios this contract owns

| # | Scenario | Expected |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | `RecordsLoaded(dateRange: DateRangeOption.thisWeek)`, download icon tapped | `ExportSheet` is constructed with `periodStart` = this week's most-recent-Monday boundary, `periodEnd: null` |
| 2 | `RecordsLoaded(dateRange: DateRangeOption.allTime)`, download icon tapped | `ExportSheet` is constructed with `periodStart: null, periodEnd: null` |
| 3 | Download icon tapped twice in rapid succession (before the first `showModalBottomSheet` future resolves) | `showModalBottomSheet` is called exactly once |
| 4 | Sheet dismissed, download icon tapped again | `showModalBottomSheet` is called again (a fresh `ExportSheet`/`ExportBloc`, research.md R6) — not blocked by the now-`false` guard |
| 5 | Opening/closing the export sheet, at any of its states | `RecordsBloc`'s own state (`entries`, `dateRange`, scroll position via `ScrollController`) is bit-for-bit unchanged before and after (FR-010/SC-004) |

